
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Practical project tests (host-side, no hardware required):

- Decoder regression tests for `chirpstack/decoder.js`:
	- Run with Node.js from project root:
		`node test/decoder.test.js`
	- Verifies:
		- Port 1 channel mapping (including debug RF channels 205-208 and
		  the wide Power/Generic Sensor channels 11, 19, 203, 204)
		- Port 2 daily summary decoding (legacy analog and wide volume)
		- Port 3 rejects unknown protocol versions
		- Port 3 binary decoding v2 (still accepted) and v3 (widened fields)
		- PCB v2.0 I/O fields: digital inputs/outputs, 2nd flow sensor and
		  pulse counter on port 1 (ch 21-24) and port 3 (bits 28-31)

- Encoder/decoder round trip for the binary format (FPort 3):
	- Needs a C++ compiler (c++/g++/clang++; CXX overrides), skipped if none:
		`node test/payload_roundtrip.test.js`
	- Compiles src/payload_binary.cpp with test/payload_roundtrip.cpp for
	  the host, encodes known measurement sets (full, minimal, out of range)
	  and checks decoder.js returns the same values (and clamps, not wraps).
